 "chapters": [
  {
   "id": "ryland-maxwell-jets",
   "kind": "chapter",
   "club": "Jets",
   "headline": "A Ring in New York Before Anyone Knew His Name",
   "body": [
    "Ryland Maxwell's first ring came in Y80, when Dorren Skura's Jets went 15-2 and beat the Seahawks 28-26 in Super Bowl CXXXIX. Maxwell was part of it and nowhere near the center of it. His card closed that season rated 62 with a C grade, and the market valued it at 7, the kind of price reserved for depth.",
    "Y81 brought 1,284 rushing yards and no title. Y82 brought both: 1,430 yards, 17 rushing touchdowns and a second ring after a 46-8 rout of the Eagles in Super Bowl CXLI, a club he would one day call home. Through three seasons in New York he had 3,514 rushing yards in 56 games and an Offensive Rookie of the Year award on the shelf. Useful. Not yet a reason to build a franchise around him."
   ],
   "players": [
    "Ryland Maxwell"
   ],
   "teams": [
    "Jets",
