  {
   "id": "ryland-maxwell-left-behind",
   "kind": "chapter",
   "club": "Falcons",
   "headline": "Left Behind in Atlanta",
   "body": [
    "Then Skura moved on to Philadelphia for Y88, and Maxwell stayed. The Eagles won Super Bowl CXLVII that season and CXLVIII the next, the coach's titles now arriving without the back who had carried his last five. In Atlanta, Maxwell kept running: 1,403 yards in Y88, 1,172 in Y89 and 1,223 in Y90, without a single catch in the last two of those seasons. No rings came.",
    "The market did not seem to mind. In Y88, with no title to show for it, his card passed Sawyer's for the first time, 7,837 to 7,820, and by the end of Y90 he was rated 99. The best back in the league was waiting in the wrong city."
   ],
