  {
   "id": "ryland-maxwell-eagles",
   "kind": "chapter",
   "club": "Eagles",
   "headline": "The Reunion, the Record and the Gauntlet",
   "body": [
    "In Y91 coach and back were together again in Philadelphia, and the titles came back with them: four seasons, four rings, starting with a 38-23 win over the Raiders in Super Bowl CL. Y92 brought 2,839 rushing yards, the best season on Skura's record board, and in Y93 Maxwell passed Lane McCoy's 24,507 career rushing yards to take the league record. Along the way the Eagles won 49 straight games, a run that only ended in Dallas in Y94.",
    "Y94 was a season nobody had seen before. Maxwell caught 53 touchdown passes, the most in a season on Skura's board, and was named Most Valuable Player for the first time. It was the one major award he had never won. With it he became the first player to win every one of them: a ring, the MVP, Offensive Player of the Year, Super Bowl MVP and Offensive Rookie of the Year. Ryland Maxwell ran the Gauntlet."
   ],
   "players": [
    "Ryland Maxwell",
    "Lane McCoy"
   ],
