  {
   "id": "ryland-maxwell-last-lap",
   "kind": "lastlap",
   "headline": "Two More Rings, First All Time, and One More Year at 35",
   "body": [
    "There was no argument left to settle, and he played on anyway. In Y95 he ran for 2,141 yards and won a 12th ring, playing 18 of the Eagles' 20 games after injury cost him 2, and passed Sherman Brandson for first in Career Legacy, 14,019 to 13,540. Y96, at 34, was better still: 2,574 yards and 25 rushing touchdowns in 21 games, a 13th ring after a 40-26 win over the Bengals, and a 7th Super Bowl MVP, with the career rushing record now at 32,108 yards.",
    "Then, instead of leaving on top, he re-signed with Dorren Skura. He opens Y97 at 35, still an Eagle. The Hall of Fame watch already scores him at 99, and the Hall can wait one more year."
